# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WS4 cross-modal stream — keep downloaded and regenerated data out of git.
#
# This repo ships only two things: the four notebooks, and the small curated
# per-site profiles under LINCS/data/ and OpenScreen/data/. Everything else the
# notebooks touch is an INPUT that has to be fetched:
#
#   *_cells.h5ad          Google Drive        ~2-4 GB each
#   aggregated_data/      Google Drive        raw per-well CSVs, 5 sites x 28 files
#   annotations/          Google Drive        compound + well annotation CSVs
#   LINCS/morphology/     Cell Painting Gallery S3 (266 MiB) + GitHub LFS
#
# ...or an OUTPUT the notebooks write next to themselves (lincs_expression_a549.h5ad
# is 605,940 x 62,710 — never commit that).
#
# See docs/ws4/data.md in the parent project for what each one unlocks.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- heavy data formats, wherever they land --------------------------------
*.h5ad
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.zarr/
*.parquet
*.feather
*.sqlite
*.csv
*.csv.gz
*.tsv
*.tsv.gz
*.npy
*.npz
*.pkl
*.tiff
*.tif
*.nd2
*.zip
*.gz

# --- ...except the curated profiles this repo genuinely ships --------------
# Narrow on purpose: `!LINCS/data/**` would re-include ANYTHING dropped under
# data/, and the lincs-cell-painting checkout is 1.1 GB of exactly that.
!LINCS/data/*.h5ad
!OpenScreen/data/*.h5ad

# --- downloaded input trees ------------------------------------------------
# lincs-cell-painting, 1.1 GB. It has arrived under LINCS/data/morphology/ in
# this tree; LINCS/morphology/ is where the notebook expects it. Ignore both.
LINCS/morphology/
LINCS/data/morphology/
LINCS/a549_cells.h5ad
aggregated_data/
annotations/
OpenScreen/aggregated_data/
OpenScreen/annotations/
OpenScreen/hepg2_cells.h5ad

# --- python / jupyter ------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/

# --- os / editor -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- WS4A: the merged result tables ARE the record, so they ship -------------
# `*.csv` above is a blanket ignore for downloaded profiles. These few are small
# (~250 KB total) and are what any claim in docs/ws4a/ can be checked against.
!Results/ws4a/**/*.csv
!Results/ws4a_tuned/**/*.csv
!WS4A_presentation_pack/**/*.csv
# ...but not the 120 per-task intermediates the array job leaves behind; they are
# redundant with the merged tables above.
Results/**/parts/
Results/**/units.tsv
Results/**/cache/

# LibreOffice lock files, left behind by headless pptx->pdf conversion
.~lock.*
.~*
